nd  Budget Mick Mulvaney who has said that  raising the debt ceiling might not be  the most important thing in the world we  know that Trump is no stranger to not  making good on debts but that's not  going to necessarily tell us what's  going to happen with the issue of the  debt ceiling so a few things number one  the debt ceiling doesn't account for  inflation or the size of the economy  okay so in  relation alone would mean that the debt  ceiling has to go up in raw dollars  merely to account for the real dollar  value of the debt as inflation happens  and the other issue as I mentioned is  the total size of the economy the debt  limit has to go up to represent the same  portion of the economy and a simple way  to think about this is imagine a billion  dollar debt if you have a five billion  dollar economy a billion dollar debt  means something very different than if  you have a fifty billion dollar economy  or a five hundred billion dollar economy  but those are just logistics right  there's a bigger reason that this is a  political game and not really the  important issue that many make it out to  be the US isn't really trying to pay off  the debt nor is it meant to pay off the  debt and having that in your mind as a  sort of baseline for analysis it's just  a distraction right wingers who believe  that the way to a better economy is to  pay off the whole debt are more likely  to be against raising the debt ceiling  but what really matters isn't that it's  the ability of the United States to  service the debt in other words stay on  top of payments do on the debt and to  continue funding government programs  that millions and millions of Americans  depend on if you can't service the debt  that's a different story then you start  having problems getting other entities  to loan you money which makes it so that  you have to print more money which  devalues the money and then you  basically have your own Federal Reserve  buying your debt and that's a cycle that  i